          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Geographical Location</strong><br>\nIsrael is located in the Middle East and shares its borders with several neighboring states. In the north, it borders Lebanon, in the northeast Syria, in the east Jordan, and in the southwest Egypt. It also has a coastline along the Mediterranean Sea, making it a strategically important location in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Historical Context</strong><br>\nThe relationships between Israel and its neighboring states have been heavily influenced by historical events. Since its founding in 1948, Israel has been involved in several wars and conflicts with its neighbors. These historical events have increased mistrust and tensions in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Peace Treaties</strong><br>\nDespite ongoing conflicts, Israel has signed peace treaties with some of its neighboring countries. A peace treaty was signed with Egypt in 1979, and another followed with Jordan in 1994. These treaties have improved relationships and contributed to some stability in the region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
