          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Ongoing Conflicts</strong><br>\nHowever, there are still ongoing conflicts, particularly with the Palestinians in the occupied territories. The relationship with Syria and Lebanon also remains tense, partly due to these countries' support for militant groups fighting against Israel.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Cooperation</strong><br>\nEconomic cooperation between Israel and its neighbors is an important step toward improving regional relationships. Through trade agreements and joint projects in areas like water and energy, the countries can benefit from each other and lay a foundation for further political rapprochement.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Threats</strong><br>\nMilitary threat remains a central issue in the region. Israel has one of the strongest armies in the world and also faces threats from militant groups and some neighboring states. This strongly influences Israel's relationships and security policy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
