            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>International Mediation</strong><br>\nInternational mediation plays an important role in improving the relationships between Israel and its neighboring states. The United States and other Western countries have often acted as mediators to promote peace treaties and ease tensions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Exchange</strong><br>\nCultural exchange can also contribute to improving relationships. Through education, sports, and art, people from different countries can come together and develop a better understanding of each other, which can ultimately help in reducing prejudices and hostilities in the long run.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Future Prospects</strong><br>\nThe future relationships between Israel and its neighboring states depend on many factors. Willingness to resolve conflicts, addressing historical traumas, and fostering mutual understanding are crucial for establishing lasting peace in the region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
